    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Given: The center of a circle lies on the \\(x\\)-axis and it touches the \\((0,4)\\) point. Formulating this mathematically, we obtain: \n\n\\[\n\\hookrightarrow  \\quad(x1=0) \\quad \\quad \\quad\\quad\\quad \\hookrightarrow  \\quad(x2=1)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\quad \\quad \\hookrightarrow  \\quad y1=4 \\quad \\quad \\quad\\quad\\quad \\quad \\hookrightarrow  \\quad y2=3 \n\\]\n\nWe know the radius equals distance \\(d\\) between the center \\(Z(x_z, y_z)\\) and the \\((x1,y1)\\) point:\n\\[\n\t\\hookrightarrow \\quad d = \\sqrt{( x2 - x_z )^2 + (y2 - y1)^2} = \\sqrt{(1-0)^2 + (3-4)^2}\n\\]\n\\[\n\t\\hookrightarrow \\quad d = \\sqrt{1^2 + (-1)^2} = \\sqrt{1 + 1} = \\sqrt{2} \n\\]\nThus, the \\(8/2=r\\) radius of the circle is: 2 units. Hence, our answer is \\(\\boxed{2^2=4}\\).",
