    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the radius of the circle, we need to determine the coordinates of the center and then calculate the distance from the center to either of the given points.\n\n1. **Identify the center of the circle:**\n   Since the center of the circle lies on the x-axis, it means the y-coordinate of the center is 0. Let the x-coordinate of the center be \\( h \\). Thus, the coordinates of the center are \\( (h, 0) \\).\n\n2. **Use the distance formula:**\n   The distance between the center \\( (h, 0) \\) and one of the given points, say \\( (1, 3) \\), or the other point \\( (0, 4) \\), gives the radius of the circle. Let's use the point \\( (1, 3) \\) for simplicity. The distance formula is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Distance} = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}\n   \\]\n   Substituting the point \\( (1, 3) \\) and the center \\( (h, 0) \\):\n   \\[\n   \\text{Distance} = \\sqrt{(1 - h)^2 + (3 - 0)^2}\n   \\]\n   This distance is the radius of the circle.\n\n3. **Set up the equation:**\n   Since the points \\( (0, 4) \\) and \\( (1, 3) \\) (with center \\( (h, 0) \\)) lie on the same circle, both distances should be equal to the radius. Therefore, the radius is the same for both points:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{(1 - h)^2 + (3 - 0)^2} = \\sqrt{(0 - h)^2 + (4 - 0)^2}\n   \\]\n   Simplifying the right side:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{(1 - h)^2 + 3^2} = \\sqrt{h^2 + 4^2}\n   \\]\n   Simplifying the left side:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{1 - 2h + h^2 + 9} = \\sqrt{h^2 + 16}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{h^2 - 2h + 10} = \\sqrt{h^2 + 16}\n   \\]\n   Since both sides are equal, squaring both sides will eliminate the square roots:\n   \\[\n   h^2 - 2h + 10 = h^2 + 16\n   \\]\n   Subtract \\( h^2 \\) from both sides:\n   \\[\n   -2h + 10 = 16\n   \\]\n   Subtract 10 from both sides:\n   \\[\n   -2h = 6\n   \\]\n   Divide by -2:\n   \\[\n   h = -3\n   \\]\n   So, the center of the circle is at \\( (-3, 0) \\).\n\n4. **Calculate the radius:**\n   The radius is the distance from the center \\( (-3, 0) \\) to the point \\( (1, 3) \\):\n   \\[\n   \\text{Radius} = \\sqrt{(1 - (-3))^2 + (3 - 0)^2} = \\sqrt{(1 + 3)^2 + 3^2} = \\sqrt{4^2 + 3^2} = \\sqrt{16 + 9} = \\sqrt{25} = 5\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the radius of the circle is \\(\\boxed{5}\\).",
